cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZTARE: A Local Claim-Governance Workbench for Auditable Human-Agent Research"
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the specific paper or artifact you are
  using rather than the repository as a monolith. The repository README and
  papers index point to the active paper and artifact folders. The repository-level
  citation below is provided for tooling that requires a single `CITATION.cff`
  (for example GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget and Zenodo's DOI
  minting).
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-14"
authors:
  - family-names: Alami
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare"
url: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare/blob/main/LICENSES.md"
keywords:
  - zero-trust workbench
  - claim governance
  - claim auditing
  - source readiness
  - adversarial validation
  - research agents
  - LLM evaluation
  - research integrity
  - audit trails
preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "ZTARE: per-artifact citations"
  authors:
    - family-names: Alami
      given-names: Daniel
  year: 2026
  notes: >-
    The repository is a portfolio of distinct research artifacts. Cite the
    specific paper or artifact you are using. Paper and artifact folders under
    papers/ carry the manuscript source, references, and evidence bundles where
    available.
